64-7e48beb727cb","sourceKey":"quiz:252","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"The correct order of the stages of group development is:","options":["Storming, Forming, Norming, Adjourning, Performing","Norming, Storming, Forming, Performing, Adjourning","Forming, Storming, Norming, Performing, Adjourning","Forming, Performing, Storming, Norming, Adjourning"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Week 6 — Organisational Behaviour, Communication, and Team Dynamics"}},{"itemId":"a1fe0ef7-c4a3-51a0-afe4-6f2a2093f1ef","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"7b051023-eda1-4baf-b863-7ff75329a938","sourceKey":"quiz:253","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"OB relies on which methods rather than assumptions, in line with its scientific approach?","options":["Guesswork and opinion","Observation, research, and analysis","Popular vote","Astrology"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Week 6 — Organisational Behaviour, Communication, and Team Dynamics"}},{"itemId":"4d5dabbf-62e6-59e3-96e1-cca18572f388","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"c8ecc527-c2cf-4113-be3b-60ac28be7947","sourceKey":"quiz:254","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of these best reflects the 'goal-oriented' nature of OB?","options":["The objective of OB is to improve organisational effectiveness and employee performance","OB is only concerned with profit","OB exists only to entertain employees","OB has no defined purpose"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Week 6 — Organisational Behaviour, Communication, and Team Dynamics"}},{"itemId":"5c10db5c-5c8b-585b-bcdd-bf18e81675ee","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"3ace8c96-4f2a-41d3-b0cc-849ece3a2c34","sourceKey":"quiz:255","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"OB is described as a 'dynamic field' because:","options":["It is only taught in one country","It has no practical application","It never changes","It evolves continuously as organisations adapt to environmental and technological changes"],"correctOption":3,"section":"Week 6 — Organisational Behaviour, Communication, and Team Dynamics"}},{"itemId":"10b969a4-b96a-5849-88d1-aa37b9c7440d","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"e771f93d-1e0b-4cde-acbd-efc449063a67","sourceKey":"quiz:256","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"At the organisational level of OB, which of these topics would be studied?","options":["Individual motivation","Personality and perception","Organisational culture and organisational development","Team communication"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Week 6 — Organisational Behaviour, Communication, and Team Dynamics"}},{"itemId":"5e2b49f8-62d9-50c6-b073-c0c1ce182629","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"0d26170c-df2a-4f18-95da-44decc816d1b","sourceKey":"quiz:257","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"'Application oriented', as a nature of OB, means that:","options":["OB principles are applied to solve workplace problems and improve performance","OB principles are purely theoretical with no real use","OB cannot be applied outside a classroom","OB is irrelevant to managers"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Week 6 — Organisational Behaviour, Communication, and Team Dynamics"}},{"itemId":"24562c18-a10d-53c8-b04d-02d0f93280da","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"7b99ccd8-6bd3-4d4a-b85f-3a0620fced44","sourceKey":"quiz:258","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following is a characteristic of a group, as defined in the notes?","options":["Independence among members","A single individual working alone","No shared norms or values","Common goal or objective, and interdependence among members"],"correctOption":3,"section":"Week 6 — Organisational Behaviour, Communication, a