aset"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"67737515-a77c-5ea6-bb80-4ab29bfcd119","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"ed408ff3-9397-46b6-9ca5-965dbde6338d","sourceKey":"quiz:22","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"The value of a correlation coefficient (r) ranges between:","options":["-1 and +1","0 and 1","-100 and +100","0 and 100"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"85fa6f40-9f44-5c68-8be6-3018ac2f28af","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"70e4b166-ef8f-46e0-816b-a372f803bca9","sourceKey":"quiz:23","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"If advertising expenditure increases and sales also increase, this is an example of:","options":["Positive correlation","Negative correlation","Partial correlation","Zero correlation"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"bed89e62-7c8c-5b0a-9cad-e734cf93ecc8","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"c3e4d341-f058-41a6-bc35-e01f855ad163","sourceKey":"quiz:24","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"If price increases and demand decreases, this illustrates:","options":["Negative correlation","Positive correlation","Total correlation","Multiple correlation"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"b50e99c9-efd1-5504-a79b-29b4665937dd","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"ffc5b723-c393-4f31-a30e-c4f5d675307e","sourceKey":"quiz:25","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"A correlation coefficient of r = +1.0 indicates:","options":["Perfect negative correlation","Perfect positive correlation","No relationship","Weak positive correlation"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"a26b6eaf-c15e-5059-850c-3ac71e5ebbc9","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"38c14dbf-2ff5-48d8-9558-c30a9e19bda2","sourceKey":"quiz:26","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"An r value between 0.7 and 0.9 is interpreted as:","options":["Perfect correlation","Strong positive correlation","Weak positive correlation","Moderate positive correlation"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"00dfa95b-bd80-518c-9b67-0736089ba677","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"9ace8c44-a9dd-48bc-bec3-3e6954b9c423","sourceKey":"quiz:27","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Studying the relationship between only two variables (e.g. demand and supply), assuming a linear relationship, is called:","options":["Partial correlation","Multiple correlation","Total correlation","Simple correlation"],"correctOption":3,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"4aedfa97-350e-5480-bcad-94a11a993667","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"815baf52-4866-46b9-bb88-259e4978f686","sourceKey":"quiz:28","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Studying the relationship between yield and TWO factors — rainfall and chemical fertiliser — simultaneously (Y = a + b1x1 + b2x2) is an example of:","options":["Partial correlation","Multiple correlation","Simple correlation","Non-linear correlation"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"9f26978e-0287-5eea-aa55-331cff29818c","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"a948a204-6802-41c4-b635-23d7e90a5425","sourceKey":"quiz:29","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Studying the relationship between two variables while holding all other variables constant is called:","options":["Partial correlation","Total correlation","Multiple correlation","Simple correlation"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"836c9c36-9691-5c48-adcb-0899e64bdf36","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"4296b492-d898-4394-b8c5-4e81bc389d23","sourceKey":"quiz:3","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"The formula for Total Cost (TC) is:","options":["TC = FC + (v × Q)","TC = FC × VC","TC = P × Q","TC = FC − VC"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Section A — Basic Mathematical Concepts for Management"}},{"itemId":"00a5f9b8-57a7-50cf-affd-79a90d713b66","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"ecc55d34-6041-4c9b-8071-a2943fc48bf2","sourceKey":"quiz:30","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Correlation in which the rate of change between two variables is constant is called:","options":["Linear correlation","Non-linear correlation","Partial correlation","Zero correlation"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"8d216704-239f-5c3d-9487-61695929a6f0","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"0c71da2b-9607-45a7-8f84-d0a782c7c864","sourceKey":"quiz:31","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"On a scatter diagram, points falling exactly on an upward-sloping straight line represent:","options":["Perfect negative correlation","Perfect positive correlation","Zero correlation","Weak correlation"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"5a37c13b-88bd-5d96-befd-11e0d3548498","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"11c4598e-0dcc-425e-b456-5bcfa6ff3a98","sourceKey":"quiz:32","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which method is used to calculate correlation for ranked/ordinal data?","options":["Spearman Rank Correlation","ANOVA","Pearson Correlation Coefficient","Regression Analysis"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"b0e7f568-661d-50cb-b9ae-8a3ecd9b77d1","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"a72860c6-29df-45f0-b9d9-7a5df500becc","sourceKey":"quiz:33","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"In the class worked example, a manager recorded advertising expenditure (x) and sales (y) over 5 months: x = 1,2,3,4,5 and y = 2,4,5,8,9. What is Σxy?","options":["110","95","90","102"],"correctOption":3,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"19787b4c-273f-51be-b7b3-d99e93722d17","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"eb8702ae-3b20-4e78-a612-ffdd67f6212f","sourceKey":"quiz:34","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"In the class worked example, a manager recorded advertising expenditure (x) and sales (y) over 5 months: x = 1,2,3,4,5 and y = 2,4,5,8,9. What is Σx²?","options":["50","45","55","60"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"a48a9809-d065-52f1-8fc0-1f64defb708b","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"ef0c16f6-ecc0-4a44-b9b4-30a3a9be336e","sourceKey":"quiz:35","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"In the class worked example, a manager recorded advertising expenditure (x) and sales (y) over 5 months: x = 1,2,3,4,5 and y = 2,4,5,8,9. What is Σy²?","options":["180","170","190","200"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"52e80110-fec3-5a23-9a07-73b5b7cdc044","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"384f030e-6e3e-4c6a-9397-8f87c958e736","sourceKey":"quiz:36","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"In a class worked example applying Pearson's formula to 5 months of advertising expenditure and sales data, the result was r ≈ 0.988. This indicates:","options":["No relationship","A strong positive relationship","A weak negative relationship","A perfect negative relationship"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"f2bf6bc1-5be6-579d-b040-e6b3f40824ba","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"58a6e464-954a-427d-886f-22645fba661b","sourceKey":"quiz:37","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"The fact that ice cream sales and shark attacks both rise in summer (with warm weather being the real cause of both) illustrates the danger of:","options":["Assuming correlation implies causation","Data quality issues","Small sample size","Confirmation bias"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"36392904-03bf-5552-8c30-3215d1931f88","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"1831aecc-0eb6-4025-9156-e1f728049574","sourceKey":"quiz:38","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of these is NOT listed as a business application of correlation analysis in the class notes?","options":["Assisting in forecasting and business planning","Determining criminal liability in a court case","Studying price and demand relationships","Studying the relationship between sales and advertising"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"d1705232-743c-5620-8f8e-29316074236f","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"1631f500-de81-4d1d-be19-9c0bbced9c94","sourceKey":"quiz:39","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Studying the relationship among ALL variables simultaneously, without holding any constant, is called:","options":["Simple correlation","Partial correlation","Non-linear correlation","Total correlation"],"correctOption":3,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"0665a3b5-471b-56af-b729-3e3fc292e572","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"5373e57e-dd76-4712-ae2c-7910b50