ages for a full population census","Collecting primary data only"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Section E — Statistical Analysis: Distributions & Hypothesis Testing"}},{"itemId":"1a9e963d-4ccc-570f-bf46-edc778c211a2","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"e9feb1fa-c018-48b3-a291-55bdcaee2995","sourceKey":"quiz:63","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"The Mean (x̄) is calculated as:","options":["Middle value when data is sorted","x̄ = Σx / n","Value with highest frequency","Max − Min"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Section E — Statistical Analysis: Distributions & Hypothesis Testing"}},{"itemId":"80a4eaae-e13a-5a4e-a88f-978b5123e142","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"866ec4ad-84ea-454d-8508-be6d83f352f3","sourceKey":"quiz:64","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which measure is defined as “the middle value when data is sorted”?","options":["Variance","Median","Mode","Mean"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Section E — Statistical Analysis: Distributions & Hypothesis Testing"}},{"itemId":"a0438954-a66a-5646-9dad-4bf6b02a7063","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"26cdd8e0-c20c-4dd4-b2b6-b2de2fc1c756","sourceKey":"quiz:65","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"The Z-score formula is:","options":["Z = σ / (X − μ)","Z = μ / X","Z = (X − μ) / σ","Z = (X − μ) × σ"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Section E — Statistical Analysis: Distributions & Hypothesis Testing"}},{"itemId":"9c05d325-0d75-5bd9-ad30-24cf0e22de4c","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"f612ba31-a8f5-4105-b687-c611cccef2ed","sourceKey":"quiz:66","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"According to the 68-95-99.7 rule, what percentage of values fall within 2 standard deviations of the mean?","options":["95%","99.7%","68%","50%"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Sec